  "review": {
    "summary": "No substantive defects found in the no-project recovery change in page.tsx and page.test.tsx. The early return for no selected project now renders a PageHeader and a Card. The card has an h2 and two descriptive links: \"建立專案\" goes to /projects/new and \"選擇既有專案\" goes to /projects. The manager guard, context and scope calls run before this point and are unchanged, and the selected-project branch is unchanged too. The early return happens before getCsrfToken is called, so no form nonce is issued when no project is selected; the test checks this. Both aggregate=false and aggregate=true go to the recovery screen, which is correct because neither has a projectId. The test for `href=\"/projects\"` includes the closing quote, so it is not falsely satisfied by \"/projects/new\". The guard-rejection test confirms the recovery screen is not reached when access is denied. The four tests match it.each(2) plus 2. On accessibility, the h2 is only correct if PageHeader renders the page's h1. I did not have PageHeader's source to check this; please confirm it rather than treat it as a defect. Two small points that are not blocking: (1) the selected-project test does not check that the CSRF token is still generated and embedded, so it only partly guards the unchanged branch; (2) the copy says to come back after choosing a project, but there is no return link or redirect back to /landing-pages/new. That would be a new requirement, so it belongs in a scope proposal rather than this task. No findings is not a claim that tests or the release are verified; I did not run anything.",
